<content>
  <section><para>The table below shows the revenue for the number of pizzas sold at a restaurant.</para>
<table>
  <tgroup cols="5"><thead/>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry>Number of Pizzas</entry>
      <entry>20</entry>
      <entry>30</entry>
      <entry>40</entry>
      <entry>50</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>Revenue</entry>
      <entry>110</entry>
      <entry>160</entry>
      <entry>210</entry>
      <entry>260</entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</tgroup></table>

<para>Which linear model could be used to predict the revenue if 4000 pizzas were sold?</para></section>
</content>
